WEBVTT

00:14.315 --> 00:16.349
Aha, mm.
啊哈，嗯。

00:24.660 --> 00:27.177
These pancakes
are delicious, Sandy.
这些煎饼
很好吃，桑迪。

00:27.177 --> 00:29.453
But what do you call
this sweet stuff?
但你叫什么
这个甜的东西？

00:29.453 --> 00:31.177
That's maple syrup.
那是枫糖浆。

00:31.177 --> 00:33.729
It's kinda like jelly
that comes from trees.
有点像果冻
来自树木。

00:33.729 --> 00:35.694
Tree jelly?
树果冻？

00:35.694 --> 00:39.694
Gross.
I prefer mine on tap.
总的。
我更喜欢我的现成的。

00:41.177 --> 00:43.280
Oww!
哇！

00:44.246 --> 00:45.487
Welcome to Bikini Bottom's
欢迎来到比基尼泳裤

00:45.487 --> 00:48.280
very first
Arbor Day celebration!
第一次
植树节庆祝活动！

00:48.280 --> 00:49.970
Barber Day?
理发日？

00:49.970 --> 00:51.280
Well, I could use a trim.
嗯，我可以使用修剪。

00:51.280 --> 00:54.522
I think she said Harbor Day,
我想她说的是港口日，

00:54.522 --> 00:56.867
to celebrate old Navy swabs
like meself!
庆祝老海军拭子
就像我自己一样！

00:56.867 --> 00:59.142
It's Ar-bor Day!
今天是植树节！

00:59.142 --> 01:02.418
It's a day to celebrate
the joy of trees.
这是一个值得庆祝的日子
树木的欢乐。

01:02.418 --> 01:05.556
But, Sandy, you've got
the only tree in town.
但是，桑迪，你有
镇上唯一的树。

01:05.556 --> 01:08.487
Correction,
I used to have the only tree,
更正，
我曾经拥有唯一的一棵树，

01:08.487 --> 01:11.901
'cause today you're all gonna
grow your own tree.
因为今天你们都会
种植你自己的树。

01:11.901 --> 01:12.935
- Ah.
- Ooh.
- 啊。
- 哦。

01:12.935 --> 01:15.246
Trees don't grow underwater.
树木不会在水下生长。

01:15.246 --> 01:17.004
Oh, these little
fellers will.
哦，这些小
伙计们会的。

01:17.004 --> 01:19.453
I've used the power of science
我运用了科学的力量

01:19.453 --> 01:21.418
to make special acorns
that will grow
制作特殊的橡子
会成长的

01:21.418 --> 01:23.694
into saltwater trees,
进入咸水树，

01:26.418 --> 01:30.246
Oh, aww.
Hello, little tree.
哦，哇。
你好，小树。

01:30.246 --> 01:32.729
There you go.
Ooh, look at that.
就这样吧。
哦，看看那个。

01:32.729 --> 01:35.039
Oh.
哦。

01:35.039 --> 01:37.108
Huh? Oh.
啊？哦。

01:40.970 --> 01:43.280
Mmm.
嗯。

01:43.280 --> 01:45.798
You don't need to chew it,
you whittle stick!
不需要咀嚼，
你这个削木棍！

01:47.142 --> 01:49.246
To keep your tree healthy,
all you need to do
为了保持你的树健康，
你需要做的一切

01:49.246 --> 01:52.660
is give it lots of fertilizer.
就是给它大量的肥料。

01:52.660 --> 01:54.694
Not a problem.
不是问题。

01:54.694 --> 01:56.487
One more thing,
还有一件事，

01:56.487 --> 01:59.004
to grow a happy,
well-rounded tree,
成长为幸福的人，
树形圆润，

01:59.004 --> 02:00.522
you need to talk to 'em.
你需要和他们谈谈。

02:00.522 --> 02:03.004
- Hi, I'm SpongeBob.
- Hey, little feller.
- 嗨，我是海绵宝宝。
- 嘿，小家伙。

02:03.004 --> 02:05.280
- Testing, testing.
- Hello.
- 测试，测试。
- 你好。

02:07.867 --> 02:11.211
I love talking to someone
who knows how to keep a secret.
我喜欢和某人说话
谁知道如何保守秘密。

02:12.694 --> 02:16.177
I can finally tell someone
what really happened
我终于可以告诉别人
到底发生了什么

02:16.177 --> 02:19.211
when I pulled that job
in Shell City.
当我撤掉那份工作时
在贝壳城。

02:19.211 --> 02:20.556
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

02:20.556 --> 02:22.349
Don't worry little fella.
别担心小家伙。

02:22.349 --> 02:25.246
You'll have lots
of people talking to you.
你会有很多
与你交谈的人。

02:25.246 --> 02:27.280
Excuse me.
打扰一下。

02:27.280 --> 02:30.246
I would like to speak
to the proprietor.
我想发言
给业主。

02:30.246 --> 02:32.108
The complaint department's
over there.
投诉部门的
在那儿。

02:32.108 --> 02:34.418
Talk to the tree.
和树说话。

02:34.418 --> 02:37.280
Mr. Tree,
the condiment distribution
树先生，
调味品分配

02:37.280 --> 02:39.763
of my patty is subpar.
我的肉饼很差劲。

02:39.763 --> 02:42.522
Hm, if talking
to a tree is good for it,
嗯，如果说话的话
对一棵树来说是有好处的，

02:42.522 --> 02:47.177
I'll bet a little smooth jazz
must be amazing.
我打赌会是一点流畅的爵士乐
一定很神奇。

02:55.211 --> 02:56.729
Ho-ho!
嗬嗬！

02:56.729 --> 03:00.108
I'll talk to you
the way nature intended,
我会和你谈谈
自然的方式，

03:00.108 --> 03:03.004
with television!
有电视！

03:03.004 --> 03:06.487
<i>We now return to
"My Mother the Barnacle.</i>
<i>我们现在回到
“我的藤壶妈妈。</i>

03:06.487 --> 03:10.280
Ha-ha-ha!
I love this one!
哈哈哈！
我喜欢这个！

03:11.798 --> 03:14.073
Who's a cutesy wittle tree?
谁是可爱的智慧树？

03:14.073 --> 03:16.729
You are!
你是！

03:17.522 --> 03:19.935
Would you like to hear
a bedtime story?
你想听吗
睡前故事？

03:21.487 --> 03:24.315
Once upon a fertilizer,
there was a mama tree,
曾几何时，肥料，
有一棵树妈妈，

03:24.315 --> 03:27.970
a baby tree, and a papa tree
who went out to the forest,
一棵婴儿树和一棵爸爸树
谁去了森林，

03:27.970 --> 03:30.935
when they suddenly met
little Goldy Lumberjack.
当他们突然相遇
小戈尔迪伐木工。

03:30.935 --> 03:33.039
Ugh, what a dumb story.
呃，多么愚蠢的故事啊。

03:33.039 --> 03:34.453
Would you put a sock in it?
你会在里面放一只袜子吗？

03:34.453 --> 03:36.970
I'm trying
to get some shut-eye.
我正在努力
休息一下。

03:36.970 --> 03:38.901
You can talk?
你能说话吗？

03:38.901 --> 03:41.453
I'm gonna name you Barky.
我会给你起名叫巴基。

03:41.453 --> 03:43.073
Let go already.
已经放手了

03:43.073 --> 03:46.867
You're wrinkling my leaves,
your filter feeding freak.
你弄皱了我的叶子
你的滤食狂。

03:50.660 --> 03:53.039
- Hello, Sandy?
- Oh, howdy, SpongeBob.
- 你好，桑迪？
- 哦，你好，海绵宝宝。

03:53.039 --> 03:55.556
How's your new tree doing?
Are you talking to it?
你的新树怎么样了？
你在跟它说话吗？

03:55.556 --> 03:57.763
I'm trying, but to be honest,
我正在努力，但说实话，

03:57.763 --> 04:00.487
I really haven't been able
to get a word in edgewise.
我真的没能做到
沿边插入一个词。

04:00.487 --> 04:02.487
My tree's been doing
all the talking.
我的树一直在做
所有的谈话。

04:02.487 --> 04:04.867
Are you feeling okay,
SpongeBob?
你感觉还好吗，
海绵宝宝？

04:04.867 --> 04:07.349
Hang on.
Barky wants to talk to you.
不挂断。
巴基想和你谈谈。

04:07.349 --> 04:10.625
Why did you leave me with
this giggling hunk o' holes?
你为何留下我
这个咯咯笑的大块头？

04:10.625 --> 04:13.798
He's dimmer than a half-watt
bulb in a power outage.
他比半瓦还要暗
灯泡停电。

04:13.798 --> 04:16.625
Well, smack my tail
and call me twitchy!
嗯，拍我的尾巴
并叫我抽搐！

04:16.625 --> 04:18.763
I'll be right there!
我马上就到！

04:18.763 --> 04:21.384
Bring me a glass of water!
Change my soil!
给我一杯水！
改变我的土壤！

04:21.384 --> 04:22.625
Look out for the roots!
- Huh?
留意根源！
- 啊？

04:22.625 --> 04:24.384
Ugh, your breath smells.
呃，你的呼吸有味道。

04:24.384 --> 04:26.315
Why are you all face
and no body?
为何你们都是一脸
没有身体？

04:26.315 --> 04:27.832
Hoo, doggy.
呼，小狗。

04:27.832 --> 04:29.591
This little shrub
is a real chatterbox.
这小灌木
是一个真正的话匣子。

04:29.591 --> 04:31.556
Get me out of this dump!
带我离开这个垃圾场！

04:31.556 --> 04:35.211
A sensitive tree
like me needs sun.
一棵敏感的树
像我一样需要阳光。

04:35.211 --> 04:37.211
Oh, it's too cold out here.
哦，这里太冷了。

04:37.211 --> 04:40.177
The sun is too bright.
Somebody get me a sweater.
太阳太亮了。
谁给我一件毛衣。

04:40.177 --> 04:41.901
I want to go back inside.
我想回到里面。

04:41.901 --> 04:44.694
Aww, I wanted
to make saltwater trees,
哇哦，我想要
制作咸水树，

04:44.694 --> 04:47.591
but this one's a bit too salty.
但这个有点太咸了。

04:47.591 --> 04:50.142
I wonder how everyone else's
trees are doing.
我想知道其他人怎么样
树木正在做。

04:50.142 --> 04:52.729
Ahh!
啊！

04:52.729 --> 04:55.108
I shouldn't have let him drive!
我就不该让他开车！

04:55.108 --> 04:58.522
Ahh!
啊！

04:58.522 --> 05:02.315
Eh, at least Mrs. Puff
is having a good time.
呃，至少泡芙夫人
玩得很开心。

05:02.315 --> 05:04.039
Excuse me,
打扰一下，

05:04.039 --> 05:06.694
but this Krabby Patty
tastes awful.
但是这个蟹肉饼
味道很糟糕。

05:06.694 --> 05:08.763
Well, you look awful,
嗯，你看起来很糟糕，

05:08.763 --> 05:10.246
but you don't
hear me complaining.
但你不
听我抱怨。

05:10.246 --> 05:13.039
Oh, I am offended!
哦，我生气了！

05:13.039 --> 05:15.280
And offensive!
并且具有攻击性！

05:15.280 --> 05:18.763
Oh, PU, what stinks?
哦，PU，什么臭？

05:18.763 --> 05:21.315
Is that the customers,
or has the garbage man
是顾客，
或者有垃圾工

05:21.315 --> 05:22.625
started making deliveries?
开始送货了吗？

05:22.625 --> 05:24.315
Huh?
啊？

05:24.315 --> 05:26.625
I'm outta here!
我要离开这里了！

05:26.625 --> 05:28.349
This used to be
a respectable place.
这曾经是
一个受人尊敬的地方。

05:28.349 --> 05:29.694
People are complaining
人们在抱怨

05:29.694 --> 05:32.935
about me complaint department
complaining!
关于我 投诉部门
抱怨！

05:35.453 --> 05:37.935
Agh, what is
that horrible noise?
啊，什么是
那可怕的噪音？

05:37.935 --> 05:40.970
You should register that thing
as a lethal weapon.
你应该注册那个东西
作为致命武器。

05:40.970 --> 05:42.004
What?
什么？

05:42.004 --> 05:43.418
It's okay, buddy.
没关系，伙计。

05:43.418 --> 05:44.832
Talent isn't everything.
天赋并不是一切。

05:44.832 --> 05:48.453
- Huh.
- In your case, it's nothing.
- 嗯。
- 就你而言，这没什么。

05:52.901 --> 05:58.935
<i>And now back to "The Sir
Urchin Snail Fail Show!"</i>
<i>现在回到“先生
海胆蜗牛失败秀！”</i>

05:58.935 --> 06:00.970
<i>Why you!</i>
<i>为什么是你！</i>

06:00.970 --> 06:03.729
<i>What I do?</i>
<i>我做什么？</i>

06:03.729 --> 06:06.625
Yeesh, I'm just one day old,
是的，我才出生一天，

06:06.625 --> 06:10.177
and even I can see
this show is for babies.
甚至我也能看到
这个节目是给婴儿看的。

06:12.625 --> 06:15.280
You don't get it, do you?
你不明白，是吗？

06:15.280 --> 06:17.039
Get what?
得到什么？

06:17.039 --> 06:19.142
Hey!
嘿！

06:23.660 --> 06:26.142
Out you go!
你出去吧！

06:26.142 --> 06:28.487
Huh.
呵呵。

06:28.487 --> 06:31.211
I'm free!
我自由了！

06:31.211 --> 06:33.832
Ahh!
啊！

06:36.660 --> 06:40.039
This joyride is over!
这次欢乐之旅结束了！

06:42.867 --> 06:45.556
Does this mean
I don't get my license?
这是否意味着
我没有拿到驾照？

06:53.246 --> 06:55.073
Hello, police department?
你好，警察局吗？

06:55.073 --> 06:58.073
I got a lead
on that Shell City job.
我有领先优势
从事贝壳城的工作。

07:00.211 --> 07:03.211
Hey, Squidward,
your barber called.
嘿，章鱼哥，
你的理发师打来电话。

07:03.211 --> 07:04.935
He said he's sorry!
他说他对不起！

07:04.935 --> 07:08.901
Philistine!
庸俗！

07:10.591 --> 07:15.142
Come on, boys.
Let's have some fun.
来吧，孩子们。
让我们玩得开心吧。

07:21.970 --> 07:23.315
Hmm.
唔。

07:27.108 --> 07:28.660
Glug glug glug--
咕噜咕噜咕噜——

07:28.660 --> 07:31.211
hey, buddy, wait your turn!
嘿，伙计，等你来！

07:31.211 --> 07:33.625
Ahh!
啊！

07:36.108 --> 07:37.625
Relax.
放松。

07:37.625 --> 07:40.211
This will help you grow
big and strong.
这将帮助你成长
大而强。

07:45.556 --> 07:48.073
Hey!
嘿！

07:53.935 --> 07:56.660
Whaa!
哇！

08:01.522 --> 08:03.073
- Huh?
- Thank you!
- 啊？
- 谢谢你！

08:03.073 --> 08:04.591
So long, chump!
再见，笨蛋！

08:04.591 --> 08:06.108
There she is!
她在那儿！

08:06.108 --> 08:09.280
This Arbor Day anarchy
is all her fault!
这个植树节无政府状态
都是她的错！

08:09.280 --> 08:12.522
Those trees
are ruining everything!
那些树
正在毁掉一切！

08:12.522 --> 08:15.142
Ah, agh!
啊啊啊！

08:15.142 --> 08:16.556
I gotta go.
我得走了。

08:16.556 --> 08:20.349
Hey, they're made of wood.
I say we burn them.
嘿，它们是木头做的。
我说我们烧掉它们。

08:20.349 --> 08:22.832
- Yeah!
- Yeah, burn 'em!
- 是的！
- 是的，烧掉它们！

08:22.832 --> 08:26.280
Squidward, that's not
the spirit of Arbor Day.
章鱼哥，这不是
植树节精神。

08:26.280 --> 08:28.315
Everyone, calm down!
大家冷静点！

08:28.315 --> 08:30.625
I've got a plan.
我有一个计划。

08:36.108 --> 08:38.418
Hm, ah!
嗯，啊！

08:38.418 --> 08:39.901
Ooh.
哦。

08:39.901 --> 08:43.867
Come one,
come all to Log-a-palooza!
来一个，
都来Log-a-palooza吧！

08:43.867 --> 08:47.004
It's an Arbor Day extravaganza!
这是一场植树节盛宴！

08:47.004 --> 08:49.004
All you can eat fertilizer!
肥料都可以吃！

08:49.004 --> 08:52.177
If you're a tree,
you get in free.
如果你是一棵树，
你可以免费进入。

09:01.418 --> 09:02.970
Howdy, folks!
各位好！

09:02.970 --> 09:05.522
Are your roots too wrinkly?
你的根部太皱了吗？

09:05.522 --> 09:07.832
Are your leaves feeling wilted?
你的叶子感觉枯萎了吗？

09:07.832 --> 09:10.935
Hmm, my bark is feeling
a little rough.
嗯，我的吠叫感觉
有点粗糙。

09:10.935 --> 09:13.832
Then try my wonderful
makeover machine,
那就试试我的精彩
改造机、

09:13.832 --> 09:16.280
the Arbor Revitalizer!
乔木再生剂！

09:16.280 --> 09:20.591
Look your best this Arbor Day!
Do I have any volunteers?
今年植树节，展现最美的自己！
我有志愿者吗？

09:20.591 --> 09:23.660
Yeah, I'll give
your dumb machine a try.
是的，我会给
试试你的笨机器。

09:35.694 --> 09:38.142
Run for your leaves!
跑去寻找你的叶子！

09:38.142 --> 09:39.453
Everyone wait!
大家等着吧！

09:39.453 --> 09:41.384
I love it!
我喜欢它！

09:41.384 --> 09:44.729
I was destined to rot
in the woods somewhere,
我注定要腐烂
在某处树林里，

09:44.729 --> 09:46.798
but look at me now!
但现在看看我！

09:46.798 --> 09:48.729
I'm a chair!
我是一把椅子！

09:48.729 --> 09:52.487
I've never felt so smooth.
我从未感觉如此顺利。

09:52.487 --> 09:54.729
- Whoa.
- Phew.
- 哇哦。
- 唷。

09:54.729 --> 09:56.556
He does look pretty handsome.
他看起来确实很帅。

09:56.556 --> 09:58.315
I want to be a chair too.
我也想当椅子

09:58.315 --> 09:59.970
I want to be a credenza!
我想成为一个书柜！

09:59.970 --> 10:02.142
- I want to be a sawhorse!
- I want to be a table!
- 我想成为锯木架！
- 我想成为一张桌子！

10:02.142 --> 10:04.246
- Me!
- Me next, me next!
- 我！
- 下一个是我，下一个是我！

10:04.246 --> 10:06.384
Wow!
哇！

10:06.384 --> 10:07.798
Whoo-hoo!
呼呼！

10:21.660 --> 10:24.832
These guys are great!
这些家伙太棒了！

10:27.625 --> 10:29.280
Good thinking, Sandy.
好主意，桑迪。

10:29.280 --> 10:32.315
Furniturizing really calmed
these trees down.
家具真的很平静
这些树倒下了。

10:32.315 --> 10:34.418
Ah!
啊!

10:34.418 --> 10:37.108
both: Yeah, chairs rule!
两人：是的，椅子统治！

10:37.108 --> 10:39.418
Well, most of them anyway.
好吧，无论如何，大多数都是这样。

10:39.418 --> 10:42.867
I think I'll skip Arbor Day
next year.
我想我会跳过植树节
明年。

我想我会跳过植树节
明年。